Subject: CPMS I03 Conformance Corpus Coverage Design

@ [design_uuid] 00be2d31-067e-4eb9-a050-5363571aca70
@ [profile] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\CPMS_I03_Residual_Conformance_Profile.sop

& [CorpusUnit] is one immutable root-qualified case
  + identity is domain-separated digest of profile root direction case family exact bytes expectation and fixture lineage
  + one case names ingress schema serde optional semantic and residual expectations separately
  + mutation creates a successor case identity and never rewrites admitted expectation history

& [RootMatrix] has five independent columns
  + prepare_input maps exact bytes to PrepareRequest deserialization
  + run_input maps exact bytes to PreparedRunRequest deserialization
  + verify_input maps exact bytes to VerifyRequest deserialization
  + base_response begins from a ProcedureToolResponse value valid for the base response intended use and serializes it
  + preparation_response begins from a ProcedureToolResponse value valid for the preparation response intended use and serializes it
  + shared Rust type does not merge the two response contracts because intended use and canonical root differ

& [ReaderStates] are closed
  + not_applicable accepted rejected exhausted internal_fault skipped_dependency
  + only accepted or rejected can contribute to an agreement claim
  + skipped_dependency blocks the containing proof rather than behaving like not_applicable

& [FamilyC00] canonical positives
  + minimum structurally valid document for each root where semantic completeness permits
  + representative complete I02 golden-derived fixture for each root
  + actual typed output serialization for both response roots

& [FamilyC01] faithful byte ingress
  + empty whitespace only malformed literals unterminated string invalid escape invalid UTF-8 and trailing value
  + duplicate root member duplicate nested member and duplicate after escaped-name equivalence
  + maximum bytes depth object members array items scalar count and member-name bytes below at and above
  + reader applicability is byte_ingress_only and no schema or serde reader runs after refusal

& [FamilyC02] object contract
  + each required member missing one at a time
  + each optional member omitted and explicit null where meaningful
  + one unknown member at every closed object shape
  + wrong primitive array and object type for each property class
  + wrong enum and tagged-union discriminator values

& [FamilyC03] numeric fidelity
  + i64 and u64 boundaries below at above zero negative exponent fraction and excessive token work
  + schema bounds and destination type are named independently
  + every case preserves the exact numeric token and destination Rust type

& [FamilyC04] collection and recursion
  + empty one below at above maximum list and map cases
  + procedure type and value recursion below at above semantic depth
  + JSON container recursion below at above deserializer and ingress depth
  + recursive local schema reference acceptance plus missing and escaping reference refusal

& [FamilyC05] identity digest and lineage
  + malformed empty overlong and non-ASCII SemanticId values where applicable
  + correct altered stale and mismatched digests for candidate schema argument result transcript context bundle and receipt forms
  + author validator compiler verifier Observer coordinator participant invocation and session boundary substitutions

& [FamilyC06] state transition and replay
  + generation zero stale successor same-state reversal and overflow cases
  + token holder duplicate pass nonmonotonic logical time incomplete participant set frame revision and stable-candidate conditions
  + first and replay equality plus one-field transcript result context and receipt mutations

& [FamilyC07] no-capability and refusal
  + non-executable operation provider counter external-effect counter and explicit-context-on-refusal cases
  + external reference schemes and absent retriever construction
  + completed response cannot carry refusal shape; refused response cannot carry coordination or context

& [GenerationPolicy] is deterministic and reviewable
  + hand-authored seeds establish meaning and expected disposition
  + bounded mechanical mutation may generate one-field variants only from an admitted seed and declared mutation operator
  + generator identity version input case mutation operation and output digest are retained
  + no random fuzz result enters the canonical corpus without reduction stable identity and human-reviewed expectation

& [CoverageLedger] is obligation based
  + each canonical schema rule each serde binding each residual each finite limit and each root-direction pair resolves to one or more case ids or a signed not-applicable reason
  + below-at-above obligations are counted independently
  + a case can cover several obligations but every relationship is explicit
  + coverage percentage is advisory; zero dangling mandatory obligations is authoritative

& [ExecutionOrder] is fixed
  * verify bundle and document integrity
  * run faithful byte ingress
  * run schema and serde independently where applicable
  * run explicitly named safe semantic function only on complete fixtures
  * normalize observations and compare to expectation
  * resolve coverage and residual indexes
  * repeat the entire pure evaluation and compare exact normalized report bytes

& [InitialSizeBudget] is bounded
  + no more than 4096 cases or 67108864 aggregate source bytes
  + each family begins with the smallest complete witness set and expands only from uncovered obligations
  + exhaustion yields no partial pass and preserves exact unexecuted case identities

& [ReadinessStatus] is design_complete_case_inventory_unformed
